# Who gets asked to review what.
#
# GitHub resolves an owner to a **user** or a **team** (`@org/team`). It does not
# resolve a bare organisation, which is what the placeholder `* @iritur` in the
# first version of this file was: `iritur` is the org, so every rule here matched
# and then assigned nobody, silently, for every PR since. Check this file with
#
#     gh api repos/iritur/printorian/codeowners/errors
#
# which is the only thing that would have caught it — a CODEOWNERS that names no
# one looks exactly like a working one from the PR page.

# One owner, because there is one maintainer. Per-area rules (`/backend/`,
# `/frontend/`, `/.github/`) are deliberately not written yet: with a single owner
# they would all name the same person, and four rules that resolve identically
# read as routing that is not happening. Split this the day a second person has
# write access — that is the same trigger that reopens the approvals decision in
# docs/INFRASTRUCTURE.md §7 Stage 0.
* @dimmus
